# Task: Bound every CBM tool result before it reaches Agent-Spark

## Problem (already diagnosed — do not re-investigate the cause)
Agent-Spark gap-analysis runs are slow and produce inconsistent/wrong data because individual CBM MCP tool calls return very large outputs that enter the agent's context at full size.

Verified facts (from the OpenHands SDK and CBM source):
- OpenHands `MCPToolObservation.from_call_tool_result` passes MCP text through unchanged.
- The only cap is 50,000 chars per tool message, applied at LLM serialization by middle-truncation (`DEFAULT_TEXT_CONTENT_LIMIT`). This silently drops rows.
- `LLMSummarizingCondenser` keeps recent events verbatim, so several oversized results stay in every prompt.
- Large CBM outputs come from: `get_architecture` with aspects `all`/`overview`/`file_tree`/`clusters`/`cycles` (this tool has no `max_output_tokens`); `get_code_snippet` with `source_mode: "full"`; `query_graph` with high or `0` `max_rows`; `search_code` with `mode: "full"`; and any call with large `limit`/`max_output_tokens`.

## Fix to implement
Add a CRUX-owned **bounded CBM gateway**: an MCP server that sits between Agent-Spark and CBM. Point Agent-Spark at it through Agent-Spark's existing `mcp_config`, instead of pointing it at CBM directly.

## Hard boundary
- Do NOT modify, fork, copy, subclass, monkey-patch, or wrap Agent-Spark or OpenHands code: runtime, condenser, conversation loop, tools, factory, engine, or session handling.
- Change only the CRUX/CodeMind orchestration layer, plus new gateway files.
- Do not change the gap-analysis prompt, the report schema, public APIs, durable-job behavior, fallback behavior, or UI integration.
- No unrelated refactors, placeholders, TODOs, stubs, or commented-out code.

